<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n685" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ădămantĭnus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδαμάντινος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>hard as steel</i>, etc., <i>adamantine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">saxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 447</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">duritia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 37, 11, 73</span></i>
			. —Hence <b>poet.</b>, <i>extremely hard</i>, <i>inflexible</i>, <i>invincible</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clavi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 24, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tunica,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 1, 6, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					3, 9, 9</span></i>
			; cf. aënus.</div>
